formal:
For maximum constraint satisfaction with arity \(k\ge2\) and domain size \(d\ge2\), is the achievable approximation scale
\[
q(k,d)=\frac{d\max\{k,\log d\}}{d^{k}}
=\frac{\max\{k,\log d\}}{d^{k-1}}
\]
optimal up to universal constant factors over the full two-parameter range? Here a larger factor is a better maximization guarantee, and \(\log\) denotes the natural logarithm. The source establishes an \(\Omega(q(k,d))\) algorithmic guarantee and asks for matching optimality. It does not specify a unique hardness hypothesis and algorithm-uniformity convention for the complete claim; those remaining choices are identified below rather than silently supplied.
